Port patch 0040 - cheat: Kids Club "Who wants to play?": Ready! can be chosen with nobody playing (computer against computer)
Why: a requested feature of the port (an option in the Options menu, off by default; KYUJO_CHEAT_CPUVS=1 for one run). On the join screen (MiniGameSelect_PlayerJoinUpdate) each of the four
players is a human (D_8780FA30[i] == 0, "1P") or a computer ("COM", 1); the cursor may only move from the row of players down to "Ready!" (and back) while player 1 is a human
(D_8780FA30[0] == 0), so at least one person has to join. With the cheat on the cursor moves whatever player 1 is, so Ready! can be chosen with four computers (COM vs COM vs COM vs COM): the
difficulty page (state 4) and the games themselves then run with computer players only (the games already handle computers for every empty seat). Everything else is unchanged; the host decides
(__osHostCheatOption(2), host_cheat.c).
